      "message": "NIT:\nTyping the root store as Store\u003cunknown\u003e erases both root state and getters typing for every future TS consumer of @/store.\n\n\nThe seam already has to cast (store.state as AuthRootState), and store.getters[\u0027authentication/isLoggedIn\u0027] is now any — a typo in the namespaced key (\u0027authentication/isLogedIn\u0027) would compile clean and return undefined at runtime. This locks in an untyped surface just as the codebase begins adopting TS.\n\nrecommended changes: Add at least a minimal RootState interface (extended module-by-module) or a TODO tying the unknown to the Pinia migration, so this file is not treated as the final typing for @/store",
