      "side": 1,
      "message": "NIT:\nlogout is typed and documented as if awaiting it waits for the DELETE + state clear + router redirect, but the wrapped Vuex action does not return its promise chain, so store.dispatch(\u0027authentication/logout\u0027) resolves immediately to undefined.\n\nA caller writing await authStore.logout(); router.replace(\u0027/login\u0027) (or teardown code) will race the pending DELETE and the internal router.push(\u0027/login\u0027). The commit body promises the eventual Pinia swap will be a \"no-op for callers\", so if the Pinia store later returns a real chained promise, timing-sensitive callers written against this seam will silently regress (or vice versa).\n\nrecommended changes: Either fix the underlying Vuex action to return its promise chain in AuthenticanStore.js (out of scope for this change; capture as follow-up), or tighten the JSDoc on logout to note that resolution does not imply the DELETE / redirect have completed. No change required in this patch if the JSDoc caveat is added",
